caption: Design Point Load
technology-rule: design-point-load

Design Point Load, or DPL, is the final modified character-point value of the package.

Calculate each positive trait with all applicable enhancements and limitations, then add their final costs together. For Design Point Load only, double the effective character-point value of Exotic, Supernatural, and Cinematic advantages. This design multiplier does not increase Benefit Value.

DPL determines:

Whether the formula fits within the designer’s Talent cap.

The base production cost of the chem.

Harmful side effects reduce DPL normally. This means that a short-lived, unreliable, or dangerous chem can be easier and cheaper to create than a clean version granting the same raw advantages.
